  "implementation_audit": {
    "entropy_boundary": "Entropy summarizes posterior classification uncertainty; it is not individual classification accuracy and does not correct hard-classification measurement error.",
    "lta_invariance_boundary": "Full measurement invariance is a tested modeling choice, not a universal prerequisite; partial invariance and the actual constrained parameters must be reported.",
    "ms_lta_boundary": "The Chapter 7 replay has four waves. A two-wave MS-LTA should be treated as an explicitly justified extension or constraint, not silently presented as canonical multi-wave evidence.",
    "finite_stayer_constraint": "Finite logit values such as -10/+20 approximate 0/1 transition probabilities; they are not mathematically identical to fixed probabilities.",
    "estimand_contract": "The replay separates MplusAutomation template generation, licensed Mplus estimation, readModels parsing, and R-side glm/HC0 estimation. Each stage must retain input/output hashes and state whether the estimand is latent-probability, most-likely-class descriptive, or hard-classification logistic.",
    "syntax_correction": "q1604 uses c1(4) and c3(4), yielding 16 joint combinations; q1629 uses G(2) with c1(4) and c3(4), yielding 32 joint combinations. These are not eight- or ten-class single latent variables."
